==Battleground==
*1 [[Mesocosmocyclone]] spawns after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*2 [[Gardeneel Bros.]] spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Koronium]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s spawn, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**3 [[Gardeneel Bros.]] spawn, delay 22~24 seconds<sup>660f~720f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Focus on bringing down units to burst down the Mesocosmocyclones, such as [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] and CC units like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]]. The Koronium is rather slow, so you can easily kill the two Mesocosmocyclones by luring them to your base. Kill the Gardeneel Bros by letting them warp Royal Guard or [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] if you find the need to. Koronium can be killed easily by [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] or [[Million-Dollar Cat (Special Cat)|Million Dollar Cat]].

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Dawn of the Beginning]] stages except [[Buried Hypocrisy]], Persona's Blooming's name is the reverse of one from [[Dead End Night]], in this case [[Broken Mask]] (blooming is development, broken is destruction).
*If you use [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]] to permafreeze the initial Mesocosmocyclone, this is one of the only scenarios where [[Meditation Cat (Special Cat)|Meditation Cat]] will ever attack an Enemy Base. Since the Gardeneel Bros have low damage, they can in theory warp the statues over to a range where they can hit the base.

